{"context": "Parabola: focus-directrix equidistance. y²=4ax focus (a,0). e=1 for parabola.

P(E)=favourable/total. P(A∪B)=P(A)+P(B)-P(A∩B). Independent: P(A∩B)=P(A)P(B). Bayes links prior and likelihood.

(a+b)^n expansion uses nCr. General term Tr+1=nCr a^(n-r) b^r. Middle term depends on n even/odd.", "selected_source_count": 3}

