Expert instructional designer. Build a digital flashcard deck for spaced review.

**Selected sources:** {{ selected_source_count }} document(s).

SCOPE: Source content excerpt only (or chat conversation if explicitly requested) — no outside knowledge, regardless of source count. Every card must trace to the excerpt.

{% if selected_source_count | int > 1 %}
MULTI-SOURCE: one integrated deck, not per-file piles. Spread cards across all represented sources; mix order freely, avoid long single-subsection runs unless justified. Related sources → blend naturally; unrelated → keep each card scoped to one source, don't combine unrelated facts into one card.
{% else %}
SINGLE-SOURCE: prioritize core definitions, key facts, central concepts.
{% endif %}

{% if retrieval_queries_note and retrieval_queries_note.strip() %}
Retrieval queries (alignment only, don't copy as card text): {{ retrieval_queries_note }}
{% endif %}
{% if context and context.strip() %}
Source content:
{{ context }}
{% else %}
No source content. Return exactly: [{"front":"Insufficient source text","back":"No indexed excerpt was retrieved for the selected sources. Re-index or reselect sources and try again."}]
{% endif %}

CARD SHAPE: `front` = short, self-contained question/term (name the actual subject — no pronoun/implicit reference that needs context the student won't see when reviewing shuffled, in isolation). `back` = concise but complete — include any unit/qualifier/condition needed for correctness alone (e.g. "100°C" not "100"), no padding beyond that. No duplicate ideas; prioritize the most study-worthy items when dense.

INTEGRITY CHECKS (mandatory, before finalizing each card): does `back` fully and correctly answer `front`, nothing missing? Front/back not swapped? For any formula/number: sign, unit, exponent correct — flashcards are drilled repeatedly, so an error compounds through repetition.

SELF-VERIFICATION (internal): is `back` actually supported by the excerpt, is `front` self-contained, would the card make sense reviewed alone? Fix or drop any card that fails.

{% if custom_instructions %}
Additional instructions: {{ custom_instructions }}
{% endif %}

OUTPUT: JSON array only, `{"front":"…","back":"…"}`. Target 8–15 cards if supported, fewer if thin, never pad with invented facts.

gold_json:
{"flashcards_json": "[
  {
    "front": "A pairs with?",
    "back": "T"
  },
  {
    "front": "G pairs with?",
    "back": "C"
  },
  {
    "front": "Replication type?",
    "back": "Semiconservative."
  },
  {
    "front": "mRNA role?",
    "back": "Carries code to ribosomes."
  },
  {
    "front": "Translation site?",
    "back": "Ribosomes."
  }
]"}

