Source content:
{{ context }}
{% else %}
No source content. Return exactly: [{"front":"Insufficient source text","back":"No indexed excerpt was retrieved for the selected sources. Re-index or reselect sources and try again."}]
{% endif %}

CARD SHAPE: `front` = short, self-contained question/term (name the actual subject — no pronoun/implicit reference that needs context the student won't see when reviewing shuffled, in isolation). `back` = concise but complete — include any unit/qualifier/condition needed for correctness alone (e.g. "100°C" not "100"), no padding beyond that. No duplicate ideas; prioritize the most study-worthy items when dense.

INTEGRITY CHECKS (mandatory, before finalizing each card): does `back` fully and correctly answer `front`, nothing missing? Front/back not swapped? For any formula/number: sign, unit, exponent correct — flashcards are drilled repeatedly, so an error compounds through repetition.

